 "note": "Iziz's adapter for the biome fauna sheets (the city target's hyperjungle). Each family is a near-colourless sheet that the per-instance tint colours, or the wing's alpha cut-out. All are optional until the sheets are generated (core/materials/PROMPTS-ready.md). build.py's fauna_pack() turns the packed maps into HYPERJUNGLE.FAUNATEX. Since 2026-10-06 also the vernacular: the MAT keys of 69b-vern-mat.js (wood, woodV, stone, plaster, thatch, shingle, cloth ) bound in place by src/69e-iziz-matlib.js (KMAT.bindMat); grey detail maps (keep 0) the instance colour tints, means estimated from the procedural painters (judge in a render). dirt stays procedural (its grass patches are the point; ground.redsoil read flat). cloth's contrast is raised so the awning stripes stay bold under the tint. The shared Ancients MAT (white panels, rust, verdigris, board concrete, brick, salvage corrugate/timber/tarp, talus, worn panels) takes library sets too (2026-10-06): KMAT.bindMat with KMAT.ANCIENT_TILES keeps each procedural map's feature size; means and metalness measured from the procedural maps; rust, verdigris, brick, timber and the worn panels keep their own colour. verdigris keeps 60 % of its own colour. rust stays procedural: the Ancients meshes stretch their UVs along beams and tanks, and every library rust (plate, scan) smeared into stripes there, where the procedural noise was made for it.",
